- Lowercases its input: met (`.toLowerCase()`; test "lowercases text").
- Runs of characters other than a-z / 0-9 become one hyphen: met (`/[^a-z0-9]+/g` -> `"-"`; test "one -- two...THREE" -> "one-two-three").
- No leading or trailing hyphens: met (`/^-|-$/g` removal; the single-hyphen strip is sufficient because runs are already collapsed). Test covers it.
- Tests pass with `node --test`: met. I ran it: 4 tests, 4 pass, 0 fail.

Extra spot checks (behaviour is consistent with the spec): `slugify("Café Ünï 2")` -> `caf-n-2`, `slugify("A_b")` -> `a-b`, `slugify("")` -> `""`, `slugify("--a--")` -> `a`.

## Other notes (non-blocking)

- Tests are in `test/slugify.test.mjs` using `node:test`, as requested.
- No changes outside `src/slugify.mjs` and `test/`.

## Verdict

fail: acceptance criteria hold, but the mandatory `// woof-acceptance: 3193b908557a` header is missing from `src/slugify.mjs`.

